    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n45620" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">structĭlis</span></b> , e, adj.
		struo, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>of</i> or <i>belonging to building; that is
			built</i> or <i>constructed; that is designed</i> or
				<i>used for building</i> (postAug.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">canales,</span>”
				<i>walled</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Vitr. 8,
					7</span></i>
			; so, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">cloacae,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. 5, 9
						<i>med.</i></span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">columnae,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Dig.
					8, 5, 8</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">bases,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">ib. 50, 16, 245</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">opus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">ib. 50, 16, 241</span></i>
			:  gemellar, <i><span class="en">Col. 12,
				52, 10</span></i>: caementum, <i>building -
			cement</i>, i. e. <i>that is used in building</i>,
				<i><span class="en">Mart.
				9, 76, 1</span></i>.</div>
